---
description: Hardware backend ownership, protocol and write-safety rules
globs: "src/*backend*.py,src/kraken_*.py,src/nzxt_*.py,src/openlinkhub_*.py,src/openrgb_*.py,src/rgb_*.py,src/mainboard_fan_control.py,src/ohc_fan_helper.py,src/cooling_ownership.py,src/hardware_request_coordinator.py"
alwaysApply: false
---

Read @DEVICE_SUPPORT.md and @SUPPORTED_DEVICES.md before changing hardware behavior.

Do not guess USB commands, firmware protocols, PWM mappings, device IDs, LED counts or sysfs write paths. Preserve session authorization, bounds checks, process/device ownership and safe fallback behavior. Keep OpenLinkHub/OpenRGB network paths loopback-only. Real hardware validation is required before changing a device from detected/provisional to tested/supported.
